# Direct dependencies. `requirements.txt` is generated from this file and is
# the lock -- pinned, hashed and resolved for every platform this runs on:
#
#     uv pip compile --universal --generate-hashes \
#         --python-version 3.12 -o requirements.txt requirements.in
#
# Install still reads requirements.txt, so nothing about deploying changes.
#
# CI does not re-compile this to check the two agree. It would have to resolve
# against live PyPI, so the diff would fail the moment any transitive package
# published a release -- a red build caused by someone else's upload. Editing
# this file without recompiling is self-revealing instead: the package does not
# get installed, and selfcheck says so.
